1. A NetLogo agent is a "being" that you can program to do different actions. Observers provide instructions to other agents, turtles are agents that can move, and patches make up the background of the world.
2. Properties are values of agents that each agent has and that you can change. You can use the command "set" to change any of the properties of turtle and patch agents.
3. The background is made up of 1089 squares, with each square being called a "patch." The color of each patch is a property that you can change, with "pcolor" being the property associated with the color of each patch.
4. set pcolor random
5. set pcolor red orange
6. setxy randompositive randomnegative
